WEBVTT

00:02:28.472 --> 00:02:32.082
with only a 25 micrometer width.

00:02:32.082 --> 00:02:35.070
Long, fine fibers 
can wrap around one another

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.800
better than shorter, 
less fine fibers,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.740
which means those long, fine fibers 
make stronger threads

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.279
that hang together better as fabric.

00:02:44.279 --> 00:02:47.150
Cotton with these qualities 
has diverse uses—

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.090
from soft textiles 
to the U.S. dollar bill,

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:53.143
which is 75% cotton.

00:02:53.143 --> 00:02:56.058
The next crucial stage 
of the cotton fiber’s growth

00:02:56.058 --> 00:02:59.348
begins as it thickens 
its secondary cell wall

00:02:59.348 --> 00:03:04.037
by depositing large quantities 
of cellulose into the secondary layer.